 "evidence": "The GCM: 3-day means of one two-year run in the site cells (heating by process as PlaSim writes it; the diffusivity recomputed with vdiff's formula on the means, which differ from the means of the step-by-step values). CM1: domain means of one realization per box over its settled lunar day.",
 "reading_rule": "By site and quarter of the lunar day (hour angle from noon), at the GCM's half levels (z_half_m above the ground, the ground up): heat and vapour carried upward through each (W/m2). gcm.heat_w_m2 is vertical diffusion plus dry adjustment from the run's own heating, which PlaSim writes as single time steps at the end of each 3-day mean, binned here by the time of those steps (half a mean's length after its midpoint), with its share of the surface layer's heating at the same steps (sensible_at_snapshots_w_m2); every other GCM value is a 3-day mean binned by its midpoint. heat_vdiff_on_means_w_m2 recomputes the diffusion on the 3-day means as a check, and k_m2_s (the mean over the means), k_median_m2_s, k_stretched_m2_s (mixing lengths times stretch), ri_median and stability_factor place each half level's regime on the means. cm1 values are interpolated to the same heights, the resolved part (thfr, qvfr), the advection's implicit diffusion (thfd, qvfd) and the boundary-layer scheme's subgrid part (thfs, qvfs) beside the total; k_effective_vapour_m2_s is the vapour flux over the mean gradient where vapour falls by at least 0.05 g/kg per km. Shares divide by the surface's sensible or latent heat. mixed_depth_m: the first height above the GCM's lowest full level where the mean virtual potential temperature has risen 0.5 K above its value there. Profiles at the GCM's full levels (z_full_m), theta_v referred to 1000 hPa, vapour as a mixing ratio in both models.",
